{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c91ef6abc03608ad","name":"The Invisible Hand","source":{"id":"source:reference-c91ef6abc03608ad","title":"The Invisible Hand","revision":20068,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:08:38Z","sha256":"8e91ddac11d7d29eba3c248cd1a3e0d73d08282c66d4138b077163175c73df2f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20068","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Invisible%20Hand&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c91ef6abc03608ad","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Invisible Hand"]}," is the personal flagship of ",{"tag":"a","children":["General Grievous"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/General_Grievous","referenceId":"reference:ff638626530ef283"}," and is used in at least twenty-six massive naval attacks on Loyalist worlds, including ",{"tag":"a","children":["Belderone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Belderone?action=edit&redlink=1"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Humbarine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Humbarine?action=edit&redlink=1"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Duro"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Duro","referenceId":"reference:649f085c70b1304a"},", and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},". It also deploys a deadly brain plague that killed nearly every ",{"tag":"a","children":["Republic Clone"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Republic_Clone","referenceId":"reference:bc69b18c7ceccecb"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," in the entire Weemall Sector. During ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," this quickly became one of the most feared Separatist vessels next to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Malevolence"]}],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Subjugator-Class_Heavy_Cruiser","referenceId":"reference:428a83071e692165"},", causing ",{"tag":"a","children":["Republic Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Republic_Intelligence"}," to desperately try to locate and destroy it.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Of course, Grievous instead has its sister ships, The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Lucid Voice"]}," and The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Colicoid Swarm"]},", act as doubles to confuse the Republic. At the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},", the ship is used by Grievous and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Count Dooku"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Count_Dooku","referenceId":"reference:28558e49506f1132"}," to capture ",{"tag":"a","children":["Chancellor Palpatine"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Chancellor_Palpatine"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["Obi-Wan Kenobi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Obi-Wan_Kenobi","referenceId":"reference:6e84377ee76928db"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Anakin Skywalker"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Anakin_Skywalker","referenceId":"reference:e7c68f75d23b428e"}," were able to rescue the Chancellor, but the ship takes too much damage and Skywalker crash-lands it on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},". What remains of the ship is irreparable.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Invisible Hand"]}," has much of its advanced sensory equipment removed, and the high sensor tower was refitted as luxury quarters for Grievous. Further, a massive hangar is installed at the loss of some speed and maneuverability. This hangar has 2,000 points and is typically equipped with 120 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Tri-Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Tri-Fighters"},", 120 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vulture Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vulture_Droids"}," and 160 ",{"tag":"a","children":["MTTs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/MTTs"},". The remaining 1,500 hangar points are used for 280 other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", including ",{"tag":"a","children":["AATs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AATs"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["IG-227 ",{"tag":"i","children":["Hailfire"]},"-Class Droid Tanks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/IG-227_Hailfire-Class_Droid_Tanks"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["OG-9 Homing Spider Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/OG-9_Homing_Spider_Droids"},", and Crab Droids of various sizes. The ship also has a miniaturized Droid Control Module.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Expert)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Invisible Hand"]}," Statistics (CL 20)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal (Cruiser) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ship"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"